  "data_abstract": "STAR\u2019s measurements of directed flow ($v_1$) around midrapidity for $\\pi^{\\pm}$, $K^{\\pm}$, $K_{S}^{0}$, p and $\\bar{p}$ in $Au + Au$ collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{NN}} = 200$ GeV are presented. A negative $v_1$(y) slope is observed for most of produced particles ($\\pi^{\\pm}$, $K^{\\pm}$, $K_{S}^{0}$ and $\\bar{p}$). In 5-30$\\%$ central collisions a sizable difference is present between the $v_1$(y) slope of protons and antiprotons, with the former being consistent with zero within errors. The $v_1$ excitation function is presented. Comparisons to model calculations (RQMD,UrQMD, AMPT, QGSM with parton recombination, and a hydrodynamics model with a tilted source) are made. For those models which have calculations of $v_1$ for both pions and protons, none of them can describe $v_1$(y) for pions and protons simultaneously. The hydrodynamics model with a tilted source as currently implemented cannot explain the centrality dependence of the difference between the $v_1$(y) slopes of protons and antiprotons.",
